    {
      "evidence_id": "pdfplumber:abstract",
      "source": "pdf_layout",
      "field": "abstract",
      "raw_text": "We prove that the module learning with errors (M-LW E) problem with arbitrary polynomial-sized modulusp is classically at least as hard as standard worst-case lattice problems, as long as the module rank d is not smaller than the number field degree n. Previous publica- tions only showed the hardness under quantum reductions. We achieve this result in an analogous manner as in the case of the learning with errors (LW E) problem. First, we show the classical hardness of M-LW E with an exponential-sized modulus. In a second step, we prove the hard- ness of M-LW Eusing a binary secret. And finally, we provide a modulus reduction technique. The complete result applies to the class of power- of-two cyclotomic fields. However, several tools hold for more general classes of number fields and may be of independent interest.",
      "extractor": "pdfplumber_section_boundary"
    },
